# Stress scene (decorrelation study, spec V-B9): the bunny cloud lit by ONE warm point light INSIDE it, no sky.
# Near-field: the target changes steeply along each camera ray and between neighbouring pixels, which is where
# the depth moves, and the mismatch of neighbouring targets that mutations remove, should matter most. The
# light sits at the centre of the cloud's bounding box: bunny_cloud_mip0.vbx maps voxel v to 0.08 v +
# (-24, -3.76, -16.64) over 577 x 572 x 438 voxels, i.e. x -24..22.2, y -3.8..42.0, z -16.6..18.4.
sceneBuilder.importScene(r'C:\research\Denoising-VolumetricReSTIR\VolumetricReSTIRData\default.obj')

light = PointLight('inside')
light.intensity = float3(400, 280, 160)
light.position = float3(-0.9, 19.1, 0.9)
sceneBuilder.addLight(light)
